>> title: Tonkotsu Broth, Instant Pot
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, japanese, stock, ramen, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> aka: instant pot tonkotsu, pressure cooker tonkotsu, pressure cooker ramen broth, tonkotsu in the instant pot, 豚骨, pork bone broth, quick tonkotsu
>> servings: 8
>> dish: tonkotsu-broth
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> pairs-with: tonkotsu-ramen
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the twenty minutes with the lid off is the whole white of it, and a broth not boiled hard there stays thin and grey
>> washing-up: the Instant Pot, a colander to drain and scrub the bones in, a coarse sieve, a container for the strained broth

>> step: The pot does the extraction. It cannot do the emulsion.
The pot does the extraction and does it in an afternoon instead of a day.

>> step: parboil 30 min, then scrub every bone
Cover @pork trotters{2%lb}(900 g; split lengthways by the butcher), @pork neck bones{2%lb}(900 g) and @pork fatback{6%oz}(170 g) with @cold water{3%qt}(2.8 L) in the #Instant Pot{}, bring to a hard boil on Sauté and ~parboil{30%min}. Scrub every bone until nothing brown or grey clings to it.

>> step: cook at high pressure 90 min
Return @&(~1)scrubbed bones{} to the pot with @water{2 1/2%qt}(2.4 L), lock the lid and ~pressure cook{90%min} at high pressure.

>> step: wait out the natural release 30 min, aromatics in
Let @&(~1)pot{} ~natural release{30%min} until the pin drops on its own, then drop @yellow onion{1%large}(halved), @garlic{1%head}(halved across), @fresh ginger{2%in}(sliced) and @scallion greens{4%stalks} into the broth.

>> step: boil hard, lid off, 20 min — this is the colour
Boil @&(~1)broth{} on the highest Sauté setting with the lid off, ~boil{20%min}, until it turns opaque and the fat stops pooling on the surface.

>> step: strain, pressing the softened marrow through
Strain @&(~1)broth{} through a coarse sieve, pressing the softened marrow and knuckle cartilage through with a ladle.
